    "reviewer": {
      "displayName": "Antonio Román Carena"
    },
    "starRating": "ONE",
    "comment": "Fui a canjear un matafuegos para realizar la VTV por un aviso en Mercado Libre, no sabía que era en el ACA Palermo, el aviso no lo dice. La observaciones en la nota de revisión de la VTV, aparece como matafuegos vencido, no sirve.\nSoy socio del ACA, lo llevé en dos oportunidades al taller mecánico, en la segunda, para antes de irme de vacaciones a Tucumán Lo dejé para que revisaran toda la parte de distribución, a mí regreso, me quedé a 100 Kms. De Tucumán, el ruleman del tensor de correa de distribución se engranó, nunca se hicieron cargo de nada.\n\n(Translated by Google)\nI went to exchange a fire extinguisher for the vehicle inspection (VTV) after seeing an ad on Mercado Libre. I didn\u0027t know it was at the ACA Palermo (Automobile Club of Argentina) because the ad didn\u0027t mention it. The inspection report states the fire extinguisher was expired and therefore unusable.\nI\u0027m an ACA member, and I took my car to the mechanic twice. The second time, before going on vacation to Tucumán, I left it there to have the timing belt checked. On my way back, I broke down 100 km from Tucumán, and the timing belt tensioner bearing seized. They never took responsibility for anything.",
